Installed-Size: PLACEHOLDER
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-venv, python3-pip, libgl1
Recommends: python3-pyqt6, python3-psutil
Section: net
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/yourname/localdiscord
Description: P2P LAN chat application with end-to-end encryption
 LocalDiscord is a peer-to-peer chat application designed for local area
 networks (LAN). No central server is needed — peers discover each other
 automatically via UDP broadcast, multicast, and mDNS.
 .
 Features:
  - Cross-subnet discovery via UDP multicast (works across VLANs)
  - Text channels and direct messages (DM)
  - File transfer with inline image preview (up to 50 MB)
  - Chat history persisted locally as JSON
  - Automatic peer discovery (UDP broadcast + multicast + mDNS)
  - Manual "Add Peer" button for direct IP connection
  - Optional relay server for restricted networks
  - End-to-end encryption (X25519 ECDH + AES-256-GCM)
  - Desktop notifications via system tray with notification sound
  - Unread message badges on channels and DMs (WhatsApp-style)
  - Discord-inspired dark-theme Qt6 user interface
  - No configuration required — works out of the box on a LAN
